      "source": "Scanned every nonzero term P_k(N) = prod_(j=1..k)(q^N+q^-N-q^j-q^-j) for N <= 12 (66 terms; k >= N vanishes identically). None lies in [1.8e-7, 2.4e-7]. Scope-(a) on 'a single term of the 4_1 cyclotomic ladder supplies the residual'; a sum over the ladder is J_N(4_1) itself and is O(1)."
    },
    {
      "name": "ladder_magnitude_floor_is_order_w_not_order_w_cubed",
      "computed": "1",
      "expected": "1",
      "passed": true,
      "tolerance": 0,
      "source": "Smallest nonzero term is N=5, k=4: 0.001146530028 = 5429.55x the residual and 0.105216x w, i.e. order w. The residual is order w^3 (t/w^3 = 0.163199). Structural: each factor is an integer polynomial in w with lowest term (N^2-j^2)w and the factors increase with N, so the floor over N > k is M_k(k+1) w^k with M_k = k!(2k+1)!/(k+1)!, which bottoms out near k=4 at ~1e-3."
    },
    {
      "name": "min_coefficient_matches_the_closed_form",
      "computed": "1260",
      "expected": "1260",
      "passed": true,
      "tolerance": 0,
      "source": "M_3(4) = (16-1)(16-4)(16-9) = 15*12*7 = 1260 = 3!*7!/4!. Guards the closed form M_k(k+1) = k!(2k+1)!/(k+1)! that the leading-order floor table is computed from, so a future edit to either cannot silently diverge from the other."
    }
  ],
